{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G9eQNwFnRCb3GcLiVZnEzN","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel01.1-uc001-cat\n     2→title: \"Concatenate and display files via cat\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go cat binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary concatenates\n     6→  input to stdout, optionally applying line numbering, blank-line squeezing, or non-printing\n     7→  character display. The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the\n     8→  Homebrew reference binary (gcat from coreutils) with the same stdin, args, and environment\n     9→  and confirms that their outputs are identical byte-for-byte. No output normalization is\n    10→  needed because cat output is deterministic.\n    11→\n    12→actor: Human Operator\n    13→\n    14→trigger: |\n    15→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd006-cat.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n    16→  a passing differential test for cmd/cat.\n    17→\n    18→flow:\n    19→  - id: F1\n    20→    step: |\n    21→      The operator runs the Go cat binary with file arguments or stdin.\n    22→      Example: printf 'hello\\nworld\\n' | ./bin/cat -n\n    23→  - id: F2\n    24→    step: |\n    25→      cmd/cat reads from each named file in order (or stdin when no files are given or when\n    26→      \"-\" is given). It applies the active transformations in order: squeeze blanks (-s),\n    27→      non-printing display (-v/-T), end-of-line marker (-E), line number prefix (-n/-b).\n    28→  - id: F3\n    29→    step: |\n    30→      cmd/cat writes the transformed content to stdout. With no flags, output is the\n    31→      verbatim concatenation of all inputs.\n    32→  - id: F4\n    33→    step: |\n    34→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/cat and gcat\n    35→      with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n    36→  - id: F5\n    37→    step: |\n    38→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n    39→      produce identical output bytes.\n    40→  - id: F6\n    41→    step: |\n    42→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    43→      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    44→\n    45→touchpoints:\n    46→  - T1: \"cmd/cat — concatenation, line numbering, blank squeezing, non-printing display (prd006-cat R1, R2, R3, R4, R5)\"\n    47→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and comparison\"\n    48→\n    49→success_criteria:\n    50→  - id: S1\n    51→    criterion: cmd/cat compiles and ./bin/cat exists after mage build.\n    52→  - id: S2\n    53→    criterion: |\n    54→      ./bin/cat file1 file2 produces identical bytes to gcat file1 file2 for text files.\n    55→  - id: S3\n    56→    criterion: |\n    57→      The differential test for default mode passes: ./bin/cat and gcat produce identical\n    58→      output on multi-file text input.\n    59→  - id: S4\n    60→    criterion: |\n    61→      The differential test for -n passes: line numbers match gcat output byte-for-byte\n    62→      (format, width, tab separator).\n    63→  - id: S5\n    64→    criterion: |\n    65→      The differential test for -b passes: only non-blank lines are numbered, matching\n    66→      gcat -b output.\n    67→  - id: S6\n    68→    criterion: |\n    69→      The differential test for -s passes: consecutive blank lines are collapsed to one,\n    70→      matching gcat -s output.\n    71→  - id: S7\n    72→    criterion: |\n    73→      The differential test for -v passes: non-printing characters are displayed with\n    74→      correct caret and M- notation, matching gcat -v byte-for-byte on binary input.\n    75→  - id: S8\n    76→    criterion: |\n    77→      The differential test for -A passes: combined -vET transformations match gcat -A\n    78→      byte-for-byte.\n    79→  - id: S9\n    80→    criterion: |\n    81→      The differential test for multiple files passes: files are concatenated with no\n    82→      separator, matching gcat output.\n    83→  - id: S10\n    84→    criterion: |\n    85→      A non-existent file argument produces an error to stderr, exits 1, and still\n    86→      processes other files on the command line, matching gcat behavior.\n    87→\n    88→out_of_scope:\n    89→  - FIONREAD ioctl optimization is not tested; correctness is the only requirement.\n    90→  - Same-file detection warning (cat reading from its own output) is not tested.\n    91→  - -u flag is accepted but has no observable effect; a test verifies acceptance only.\n    92→\n    93→test_suite: test-rel01.1\n    94→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52dc9268-38a9-408c-ad3e-30afddea9623","uuid":"6a092ebc-8697-4443-8f9d-964ad0dc5012","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/190/docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.1-uc001-cat.yaml","content":"id: rel01.1-uc001-cat\ntitle: \"Concatenate and display files via cat\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go cat binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary concatenates\n  input to stdout, optionally applying line numbering, blank-line squeezing, or non-printing\n  character display. The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the\n  Homebrew reference binary (gcat from coreutils) with the same stdin, args, and environment\n  and confirms that their outputs are identical byte-for-byte. No output normalization is\n  needed because cat output is deterministic.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd006-cat.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n  a passing differential test for cmd/cat.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go cat binary with file arguments or stdin.\n      Example: printf 'hello\\nworld\\n' | ./bin/cat -n\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/cat reads from each named file in order (or stdin when no files are given or when\n      \"-\" is given). It applies the active transformations in order: squeeze blanks (-s),\n      non-printing display (-v/-T), end-of-line marker (-E), line number prefix (-n/-b).\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      cmd/cat writes the transformed content to stdout. With no flags, output is the\n      verbatim concatenation of all inputs.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/cat and gcat\n      with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n      produce identical output bytes.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/cat — concatenation, line numbering, blank squeezing, non-printing display (prd006-cat R1, R2, R3, R4, R5)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and comparison\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/cat compiles and ./bin/cat exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: |\n      ./bin/cat file1 file2 produces identical bytes to gcat file1 file2 for text files.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test for default mode passes: ./bin/cat and gcat produce identical\n      output on multi-file text input.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test for -n passes: line numbers match gcat output byte-for-byte\n      (format, width, tab separator).\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test for -b passes: only non-blank lines are numbered, matching\n      gcat -b output.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test for -s passes: consecutive blank lines are collapsed to one,\n      matching gcat -s output.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test for -v passes: non-printing characters are displayed with\n      correct caret and M- notation, matching gcat -v byte-for-byte on binary input.\n  - id: S8\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test for -A passes: combined -vET transformations match gcat -A\n      byte-for-byte.\n  - id: S9\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test for multiple files passes: files are concatenated with no\n      separator, matching gcat output.\n  - id: S10\n    criterion: |\n      A non-existent file argument produces an error to stderr, exits 1, and still\n      processes other files on the command line, matching gcat behavior.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - FIONREAD ioctl optimization is not tested; correctness is the only requirement.\n  - Same-file detection warning (cat reading from its own output) is not tested.\n  - -u flag is accepted but has no observable effect; a test verifies acceptance only.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel01.1\n","numLines":94,"startLine":1,"totalLines":94}}}
